    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "63b93cb3_6590b017",
        "filename": "ssh/server.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 587,
      "author": {
        "id": 35051
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-20T01:57:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "On the client side, the `HostKeyAlgorithms` field can be used to select allowable signature algorithms. There\u0027s no good option on the server side -- either we support the algorithm, or we don\u0027t. This didn\u0027t matter before because you could filter by `ssh.PublicKey.Type()` in the `PublicKeyCallback`, but now there\u0027s no way to say \"I want SHA-2 RSA pubkey signatures, but not SHA-1\". I\u0027m not sure how to expose this configuration but it\u0027s clearly desirable.",
      "revId": "529275081d22a0282b1c5ccd137ffab21180d419",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ff862cdb_f568085e",
        "filename": "ssh/server.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 587,
      "author": {
        "id": 28719
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-20T01:58:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m fairly convinced that the right move is to land this with that missing knob, then decide about the knob in the future. I don\u0027t think there\u0027s any case where you are _worse off_ with this?",
      "parentUuid": "63b93cb3_6590b017",
      "revId": "529275081d22a0282b1c5ccd137ffab21180d419",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705"
    },
